H8163.strongs:
Origin: or שָׂעִר; from 8175;
Meaning: shaggy; as noun, a he-goat; by analogy, a faun
KJV renders: devil, goat, hairy, kid, rough, satyr.

H8164.strongs:
Origin: formed the same as 8163;
Meaning: a shower (as tempestuous)
KJV renders: small rain.

H8165.strongs:
Origin: formed like 8163; rough;
Meaning: Seir, a mountain of Idumaea and its aboriginal occupants, also one in Palestine
KJV renders: Seir.

H8166.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 8163;
Meaning: a she-goat
KJV renders: kid.

H8167.strongs:
Origin: formed as 8166; roughness;
Meaning: Seirah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Seirath.

H8168.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to hollow out;
Meaning: the palm; by extension, a handful
KJV renders: handful, hollow of the hand.

H8169.strongs:
Origin: or שַׁעֲלַבִּין; plural from 7776; fox-holes;
Meaning: Shaalbim or Shaalabbin, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shaalabbin, Shaalbim.

H8170.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 8169;
Meaning: a Shaalbonite or inhabitant of Shaalbin
KJV renders: Shaalbonite.

H8171.strongs:
Origin: plural of 7776; foxes;
Meaning: Shaalim, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shalim.

H8172.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to support one's self
KJV renders: lean, lie, rely, rest (on, self), stay.

H8173.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: (in a good acceptation) to look upon (with complacency), i.e. fondle, please or amuse (self); (in a bad one) to look about (in dismay), i.e. stare
KJV renders: cry (out) (by confusion with 7768), dandle, delight (self), play, shut.

H8174.strongs:
Origin: from 5586; fluctuation;
Meaning: Shaaph, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Shaaph.

H8175.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to storm; by implication, to shiver, i.e. fear
KJV renders: be (horribly) afraid, fear, hurl as a storm, be tempestuous, come like (take away as with) a whirlwind.

H8177.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8181;
Meaning: hair
KJV renders: hair.

H8178.strongs:
Origin: from 8175;
Meaning: a terror
KJV renders: affrighted, × horribly, × sore, storm. See 8181.

H8179.strongs:
Origin: from 8176 in its original sense;
Meaning: an opening, i.e. door or gate
KJV renders: city, door, gate, port (× -er).

H8180.strongs:
Origin: from 8176;
Meaning: a measure (as a section)
KJV renders: (hundred-) fold.

H8181.strongs:
Origin: or שַׂעַר; (Isaiah 7:20), from 8175 in the sense of dishevelling;
Meaning: hair (as if tossed or bristling)
KJV renders: hair(-y), × rough.

H8182.strongs:
Origin: from 8176;
Meaning: harsh or horrid, i.e. offensive
KJV renders: vile.

H8183.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 8178;
Meaning: a hurricane
KJV renders: storm, tempest.

H8184.strongs:
Origin: or שְׂעוֹרָה (feminine meaning the plant); and (masculine meaning the grain); also שְׂעֹר; or שְׂעוֹר; from 8175 in the sense of roughness;
Meaning: barley (as villose)
KJV renders: barley.

H8185.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 8181;
Meaning: hairiness
KJV renders: hair.

H8186.strongs:
Origin: or שַׁעֲרִירִיָּה; or שַׁעֲרֻרִת; feminine from 8176 in the sense of 8175;
Meaning: something fearful
KJV renders: horrible thing.

H8187.strongs:
Origin: from 8176 and 3050; Jah has stormed;
Meaning: Shearjah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Sheariah.

H8188.strongs:
Origin: masculine plural of 8184; barley grains;
Meaning: Seorim, an Israelite
KJV renders: Seorim.

H8189.strongs:
Origin: dual of 8179; double gates;
Meaning: Shaarajim, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shaaraim.

H8190.strongs:
Origin: of Persian derivation;
Meaning: Shaashgaz, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Shaashgaz.

H8191.strongs:
Origin: from 8173;
Meaning: enjoyment
KJV renders: delight, pleasure.

H8192.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to abrade, i.e. bare
KJV renders: high, stick out.

H8193.strongs:
Origin: or (in dual and plural) שֶׂפֶת; probably from 5595 or 8192 through the idea of termination (compare 5490);
Meaning: the lip (as a natural boundary); by implication, language; by analogy, a margin (of a vessel, water, cloth, etc.)
KJV renders: band, bank, binding, border, brim, brink, edge, language, lip, prating, (sea-)shore, side, speech, talk, (vain) words.

H8194.strongs:
Origin: from 8192 in the sense of clarifying;
Meaning: a cheese (as strained from the whey)
KJV renders: cheese.

H8195.strongs:
Origin: or שְׁפִי; from 8192; baldness (compare 8205);
Meaning: Shepho or Shephi, an Idumaean
KJV renders: Shephi, Shepho.

H8196.strongs:
Origin: or שְׁפוּט; from 8199;
Meaning: a judicial sentence, i.e. punishment
KJV renders: judgment.

H8197.strongs:
Origin: or שְׁפוּפָן; from the same as 8207; serpent-like;
Meaning: Shephupham, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shephuphan, Shupham.

H8198.strongs:
Origin: feminine from an unused root meaning to spread out (as a family; see 4940);
Meaning: a female slave (as a member of the household)
KJV renders: (bond-, hand-) maid(-en, -servant), wench, bondwoman, womanservant.

H8199.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to judge, i.e. pronounce sentence (for or against); by implication, to vindicate or punish; by extenssion, to govern; passively, to litigate (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: avenge, × that condemn, contend, defend, execute (judgment), (be a) judge(-ment), × needs, plead, reason, rule.
